Option: keep the structure — put the row-model guard + rates lookup + cost-null check inside `priceRowInPlace` and TEST the cost==null path... it's unreachable, can't test. So priceRowInPlace would have an uncovered branch → CRAP ~12 > 8 (new helper) → FAIL.

Alternative: restructure so no dead check is carried: my earlier plan:
```js
function priceRowInPlace(row, pricing) {
   var rates = row && row.model != null ? ratesFor(pricing, row.model) : null;
   if (!rates) return false;
   row.cost = rowCost(row, rates);
   return row.cost != null;
